feat(web): play Kinescope through the video provider extension point

The open-source build registers no extra video providers, so a stored
Kinescope video (an external video activity or an Embed block) shows "This
video can't be played here" or a bare iframe: no progress, completion, resume
or notes clock.

Register Kinescope in the open-source provider list
(`@ee/components/Video/videoProviders`, the ee-stub). The provider
(providers/kinescope.ts, new) matches share and embed links with the API's
rule (lib/media/kinescope.ts, new) and lazy-loads KinescopePlayer (new), which
drives Kinescope's IFrame Player API (player.kinescope.io/latest/iframe.player.js)
through ExternalPlayerProps the way the Vimeo player does: progress, the end,
trim, resume, playback rate and the seek/getTime controls. Paste detection,
Embed blocks, badges and hints pick it up from the registry; the Kinescope
badge tone and the Video.tsx note come back from learnhouse/learnhouse#1352.
An Enterprise build replaces the stub, and its own Kinescope player with it.

Covered by `kinescope.test.mjs`; `video-providers.test.mjs` and
`editor-blocks.test.mjs` keep passing.
